# Milestone: M3
# Covers: a function call (OP_CALL) hits a safepoint at call-frame-push;
#         a non-top-level OP_RET hits a safepoint at frame-pop; both
#         decrement safepoint_budget_remaining correctly.
#
# blocked: per-call budget-decrement is a scheduler internal, verified by C
#          unit tests, not a chk target.  Asserting the before/after decrement
#          around an OP_CALL/OP_RET safepoint would need a public
#          safepoint_budget_remaining read accessor frozen into the v1.0 API
#          solely to drive a golden-diff fixture — rejected on API-minimalism
#          grounds.  Function-call frame push/pop correctness IS covered in
#          C, by tests/rt/test_strand.c (push_frame_grows_stack_for_max_reg,
#          nested_frames_grow_stack_and_preserve_upvals,
#          pop_frame_closes_its_upvals) and end to end by
#          tests/rt/test_exec.c::deep_recursion_and_reclaim at 10000
#          frames.  There is no C-level coverage of the BUDGET accounting
#          around a call, which is the half this fixture was about -- and
#          there is nothing to cover: only backward jumps spend budget.
# matrix-row: scheduler-safepoint
